# Block Patterns Rules

## ⚠️ **Critical: Always Run Commands in Theme Directory**
```bash
cd wp-content/themes/chairforce/
```

## How Block Patterns Work in Chairforce

### **Pattern Discovery**
- **Auto-registration**: WordPress automatically discovers patterns in `/patterns/` directory
- **No manual registration**: Just place PHP files with proper metadata comments
- **Theme categories**: Theme registers custom categories (elements, section, stats)

### **Pattern Organization**
```
patterns/
├── hero-*.php             # Hero section patterns
├── content-*.php          # Content layout patterns
├── section-*.php          # Section patterns
├── elements-*.php         # UI element patterns
└── all-patterns.php       # Demo pattern showcase
```

## How to Create Block Patterns

### **Theme Asset References**
**Always use theme assets instead of WordPress uploads directory:**

```php
<?php
/**
 * Title: Hero Section
 * Slug: chairforce/hero-section
 * Categories: hero, sections
 */
?>
<!-- wp:cover {"url":"<?php echo esc_url( get_theme_file_uri( 'src/assets/images/dark-headshot-bg.png' ) ); ?>","alt":"placeholder-hero-large-bg"} -->
<div class="wp-block-cover">
    <!-- wp:heading {"level":1,"textAlign":"center"} --><h1 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center">Hero Title</h1><!-- /wp:heading -->
    <!-- wp:paragraph {"align":"center"} --><p class="has-text-align-center">Hero description text goes here.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
</div><!-- /wp:cover -->
```

**Why theme assets:**
- **Theme-controlled**: Assets travel with theme, not dependent on site-specific uploads
- **Portable**: Patterns work on any site where theme is installed
- **Consistent**: Same images across all installations
- **No broken links**: Assets are always available

## How to Fix Patterns Using Upload URLs

### **Identify Upload References**
Look for these patterns in existing pattern files:
- `wp_get_attachment_url()` calls
- Hardcoded `/wp-content/uploads/` paths
- `get_field('image')` returning upload URLs

### **Replace with Theme Assets**
```php
// ❌ Don't use
"url":"<?php echo wp_get_attachment_url(123); ?>"
"url":"/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/image.jpg"

// ✅ Use instead
"url":"<?php echo esc_url( get_theme_file_uri( 'src/assets/images/dark-headshot-bg.png' ) ); ?>"
```

### **Available Theme Assets**
Check `/src/assets/images/` for available images:
- `dark-headshot-bg.png` - Hero backgrounds
- `placeholder-*.png` - Various placeholder images
- `logo-*.png` - Theme logos and branding

### **When Images Aren't in Theme Assets**
If the required image isn't in theme assets:
1. **Ask user to place it** in `/src/assets/images/` directory, OR
2. **Auto-fetch from uploads** and place in theme assets

**Never leave external upload references** - all assets must be theme-contained.

## ACF Field Integration in Patterns

### **Using ACF Fields**
```php
<!-- wp:heading {"level":1,"textAlign":"center"} --><h1 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-center">[chairforce field="hero_title"]</h1><!-- /wp:heading -->
<!-- wp:paragraph {"align":"center"} --><p class="has-text-align-center">[chairforce field="hero_description"]</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->
<!-- wp:button --><div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link wp-element-button" href="[chairforce field='hero_cta_link']">[chairforce field="hero_cta_text"]</a></div><!-- /wp:button -->
```

### **Screen-Specific Content**
```php
<!-- wp:chairforce/screen-specific-content {"data":{"screen":"mobile"}} --><!-- Mobile-specific content --><!-- /wp:chairforce/screen-specific-content -->
<!-- wp:chairforce/screen-specific-content {"data":{"screen":"desktop"}} --><!-- Desktop-specific content --><!-- /wp:chairforce/screen-specific-content -->
```

## Pattern Categories

### **Theme-Registered Categories**
- **`elements`** - UI components (buttons, tiles, icons)
- **`section`** - Page sections and layouts
- **`stats`** - Statistics and counter displays

### **Standard Categories**
- **`hero`** - Hero sections and banners
- **`banner`** - Banner displays
- **`content`** - Content layouts
- **`post`** - Post-specific patterns

